WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.280
In 1913, Ford brought
something new to car making:

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.400
a moving assembly line.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.540
Under the old method, assembling
one car took about 12.5 hours.

4
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.720
By early 1914, the time to assemble a car

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.700
had fallen to 93 minutes.

6
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.950
Adam Smith saw the same
puzzle back in 1776.

7
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.870
Ten workers made 4,800 pins each.

8
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.120
How could ten workers make
thousands of pins a day,

9
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.860
when one alone could barely make twenty?

10
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.700
In this mission, you'll calculate
what a change in the way

11
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.370
work is organized does to output
per worker and cost per unit.

12
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.730
Then you'll see why
specialists have to trade.

13
00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.600
Your mission: find out where
all that extra output came from.
